1. An imaging apparatus comprising:

a gantry defining an examination opening and an imaging axis;

a radiation source supported by the gantry and configured to emit imaging radiation through the examination opening;

a detector supported by the gantry and positioned to receive the imaging radiation after passage through an object to be imaged;

a casing at least partially surrounding the gantry, the casing comprising a bottom portion and a plurality of mobile arched modules disposed above the bottom portion;

a guide system defining circular guide trajectories for the mobile arched modules, the circular guide trajectories extending around the imaging axis; and

a thrust assembly operatively coupled to the mobile arched modules and configured to move the mobile arched modules along the circular guide trajectories relative to the bottom portion between at least a closed position, in which the mobile arched modules cover an upper region of the gantry, and an open position, in which access to the gantry is provided.
